{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Launch a rural proofing review & suspend the use of the grey-belt test",
        "additional_details": "We want the Government\u2019s review to look into updating planning policy by recognising the primacy of Green Belt purpose, village settlement boundaries & made Neighbourhood Plans when deciding on planning applications.\r\n\r\nThe 2026 NPPF uses purposes (a), (b) and (d) to identify grey belt. Those tests address the sprawl of large built-up areas, the merging of towns and the setting of historic towns \u2014 they do not directly assess the equivalent functions of land around villages. We feel this creates a serious risk that genuinely rural greenbelt land between villages is being judged by tests that do not reflect its function. We believe villages are not spaces between towns; countryside encroachment should be a decisive test.",
        "background": "Launch a rural proofing review into the grey-belt test and completely suspend the use of the grey-belt test for villages for all planning applications pending the outcome.",
        "closed_at": null,
        "closing_date": "2027-03-21",
